    <!-- Settings: help and legal -->
    <string name="legal_privacy_title">Privacy Policy</string>
    <string name="legal_terms_title">Terms &amp; Conditions</string>
    <string name="legal_help_title">Help &amp; Support</string>
    <string name="legal_privacy_body">Home Finance keeps everything on this device.\n\nThe app creates no account, asks for no sign-in, and makes no network request. Your transactions, categories, recurring schedules and preferences are stored in a local SQLite database that only this app can read. Nothing is uploaded, and there is no analytics or advertising library in the app.\n\nA backup or a CSV export leaves the device only when you choose a destination through the system file picker. That destination is then outside the app\'s control, and its own privacy terms apply.\n\nClearing app data deletes the database contents from this device. Uninstalling the app also removes them. A copy you exported earlier is not affected.</string>
    <string name="legal_terms_body">Home Finance is a personal bookkeeping tool provided as-is, without warranty of any kind.\n\nAll financial figures are entered by you. The app performs no bank connection, no currency conversion and no financial advice. Back up your data before a restore or a clear, because those operations cannot be undone.\n\nYou are responsible for keeping any exported backup or CSV file safe and for the accuracy of the records you enter.\n\nThe app is open source; the repository\'s licence governs use of the source code.</string>
    <string name="legal_help_body">Recording an entry: open Transactions and use the add action. Choose income or expense, a category, the amount and the date. Quantity and rate are optional and are for things bought by weight or volume, such as milk.\n\nRecurring items: a schedule is a plan, not spending. Nothing is added to your totals until you mark an occurrence as paid; pausing or stopping a schedule never deletes anything.\n\nReports: choose this month, three months, six months or a year. Tap a category to open its own report for the same period.\n\nBackups: create a backup before you restore, import or clear data. A backup is one JSON file; an export is a CSV of your transactions only.\n\nIf a screen shows an error, you can retry the read without losing anything: the app never writes a partial result.</string>
    <string name="legal_in_app_note">This document is shown inside the app. No online policy page or support address is configured.</string>

